# Single-page app: every path is served by the same shell, which then routes
# client-side. Without this a cold deep link — a manifest shortcut to /events, a
# shared /horse/<id> link, or a refresh on any route — 404s before the service
# worker has ever been installed to answer it from cache.
#
# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this file. On Vercel use vercel.json
# rewrites, on nginx `try_files $uri /index.html`, on Apache a mod_rewrite
# fallback. GitHub Pages — where this app deploys today — reads none of them and
# has no rewrite rules at all; there the fallback is `dist/404.html`, a copy of
# the shell written by the `githubPages` plugin in vite.config.ts, which Pages
# returns for any unmatched path. Whatever the host, the rule is the same.
#
# Note this file is written for a host serving the app from the origin root.
# Vite's `base` is `/lady-gestion/`, so a host that reads it would also need the
# prefix here — see the `base` comment in vite.config.ts.
/*  /index.html  200
